# Code owners (LS5 §16).
#
# Review requirements for the paths where a mistake is expensive: execution
# authority, evidence integrity, release publishing, and device control.
#
# This repo has a single maintainer today, so these rules do not add a second
# pair of eyes. They exist so the boundary is explicit and stays enforced when
# more people are added — and so the security-critical paths are named
# somewhere other than a design document.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                       @exergyleizhou-ux

# ── Execution authority ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The Rust SessionActor is the sole execution, permission and evidence
# authority. Changes here can silently create a second authority.
/agent/crates/codegen/xai-grok-science/         @exergyleizhou-ux
/agent/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/extensions/science.rs  @exergyleizhou-ux
/agent/crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/               @exergyleizhou-ux

# ── Desktop authority boundary ───────────────────────────────────
# The IPC allow/deny list, artifact preview containment, session binding and
# the ACP bridge. A permissive change here is a privilege escalation.
/packs/science-desktop/src/main/lumen-authority-policy.ts    @exergyleizhou-ux
/packs/science-desktop/src/main/lumen-acp-bridge.ts          @exergyleizhou-ux
/packs/science-desktop/src/main/files/                       @exergyleizhou-ux
/packs/science-desktop/src/shared/update-policy.ts           @exergyleizhou-ux

# ── Release and supply chain ─────────────────────────────────────
